<title>PERU: Banco Wiese to pay dividends.</title>
<headline>Banco Wiese to pay dividends.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's second largest bank, Banco Wiese, will pay cash dividends of 0.041 sol per share and 0.164 sol per ADR based on 1996 profits, the Lima Stock Exchange said Friday.</p>
<p>The bolsa said in its daily report that the record date is February 19 and the payout date February 26.  </p>
<p>The dividends will total 10.3 million soles, the exchange added.</p>
<p>The report also said Banco Wiese was planning a $50 million issue of subordinated bonds, whose details would be decided by company directors at a later date.</p>
<p>((-- Lima bureau, 511 221-2134))</p>
